
# Linux Architecture Diagram


+------------------------------------------------------+
|                    User Applications                 |
|             (Firefox, Chrome, Python, etc.)          |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|                    Shell / GUI                       |
|           (Bash, Zsh, GNOME, etc.)                   |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|                 System Libraries                     |
|            (glibc, libc, OpenSSL, etc.)              |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|                    System Calls                      |
|  (open(), read(), write(), fork(), exec(), etc.)    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|                    Linux Kernel                      |                  ---------> the heart of the operating system
|------------------------------------------------------|
|  Process Mgmt  | Memory Mgmt | File System | Net   |
|------------------------------------------------------|
|  Device Drivers (USB, Disk, GPU, Keyboard, etc.)    |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|                     Hardware                         |
|  CPU | RAM | Disk | Network | I/O Devices           |
+------------------------------------------------------+




| Layer        | Responsibility                       |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------ |
| Applications | End-user programs                    |
| Shell/GUI    | Interface between user and OS        |
| Libraries    | Provide APIs to interact with the kernel |
| System Calls | Entry point to kernel space          |
| Kernel       | Core of OS (resource manager)        |
| Drivers      | Hardware communication               |
| Hardware     | Physical components                  |


The kernel acts as an abstraction layer between software and hardware.
